4.14 Safety Condition as Credal-Set Supremum

The central safety condition is not a probability of unsafe deployment, which the machinery does not produce. It is a robust epistemic bound:

$\boxed{\sup_{P \in \mathcal{K}_k} P(H_i \mid O_{1:k}) \leq \epsilon_i}$

where $\mathcal{K}_k$ is the admissible posterior credal set. Alternatively, staying entirely within belief/plausibility:

$\sup_{m \in \mathcal{M}} \text{Pl}_m(H) \leq \epsilon_H$,

but this is a plausibility bound, not a probability bound. The DST/DSmT machinery is one possible route for constructing $\mathcal{K}_k$.

