5.8 Collision Obligation (Union-Bound Surrogate)

For candidate payload $i+1$ against the current constellation $\mathcal{C}_i$:

$\mathcal{O}_1(i+1): \quad \max_{j \in \mathcal{C}_i} P_c(x_{i+1}, x_j) \leq P_{c,\text{screen}} = 10^{-4}$,

$\mathcal{O}_2(i+1): \quad U_{\text{coll}}(i+1) := \sum_{j \in \mathcal{C}_i} P_c(x_{i+1}, x_j) \leq P_{c,\text{aggregate}} = 10^{-3}$.

Interpretation. $U_{\text{coll}}$ is a union-bound surrogate, not the actual aggregate collision probability. The union probability satisfies

$P\!\left(\bigcup_j H_j\right) \leq \sum_j P(H_j)$,

with equality only under mutual exclusivity. The sum is a conservative upper bound. The threshold $10^{-3}$ is a union-bound budget, not a physical probability.

Scope of NASA threshold. $P_{c,\text{screen}} = 10^{-4}$ is the NASA CARA red / mitigation-decision threshold, confirmed in NPR 8079.1 as the baseline mitigation threshold, with a post-maneuver remediation target of $3 \times 10^{-6}$ (1.5 orders of magnitude reduction). This is an external reference value, not a universal safety threshold; architecture-specific threshold derivation remains OP4.

Chapter 6 — Formal Specification

6.1 State Space

$\mathcal{Q} = \mathcal{P} \times \mathcal{D} \times \mathcal{F} \times \mathcal{A} \times \mathcal{E} \times \mathcal{I}$.

The discrete factors give $4 \times 5 \times 3 \times 4 = 240$. The per-payload hold array $t_{\text{hold}} \in [1..N+1 \to 0..t_{\text{hold}}^{\text{max}}]$ contributes $(t_{\text{hold}}^{\text{max}} + 1)^{N+1}$. The set $C$ is redundant with $i$ on every reachable state. The discrete state-space contribution under the stated finite abstraction is $240 \cdot (t_{\text{hold}}^{\text{max}} + 1)^{N+1}$. With $t_{\text{hold}}^{\text{max}} = 10$ and $N = 26$: $\approx 240 \cdot 11^{27} \approx 3.15 \times 10^{30}$.

