Appendix D — PCR6: Full Derivation and Complexity

D.1 Conflict Configurations

Let $\mathbf{m} = (m_1, \ldots, m_S)$ be a tuple of BBAs on $G^\Theta$. A configuration is a tuple $\mathbf{X} = (X_1, \ldots, X_S)$ with $X_i \in G^\Theta$ for each $i$. The configuration is

· conjunctive if $\bigcap_{i=1}^S X_i \neq \varnothing$,
· conflicting if $\bigcap_{i=1}^S X_i = \varnothing$.

Let $\mathcal{X}_{\text{conj}}$ and $\mathcal{X}_{\text{conf}}$ denote these sets.

D.2 Conjunctive Consensus

$m_\cap(X) = \sum_{\substack{\mathbf{X} \in \mathcal{X}_{\text{conj}} \\ \bigcap_i X_i = X}} \prod_{i=1}^S m_i(X_i)$. (D.1)

This is the unnormalized conjunctive rule; it collects all non-conflicting mass.

D.3 Conflict Mass and Redistribution

Total conflict mass is

$K_{\text{tot}} = \sum_{\mathbf{X} \in \mathcal{X}_{\text{conf}}} \prod_{i=1}^S m_i(X_i)$. (D.2)

PCR6 redistributes this mass to the focal elements involved, weighted by the source masses. The contribution to $X$ from source $i$ is

$\Delta_i(X) = \sum_{\substack{\mathbf{Y} \in (G^\Theta)^{S-1} \\ X \cap \bigcap_j Y_j = \varnothing}} \frac{m_i(X)^2 \prod_j m_j(Y_j)}{m_i(X) + \sum_j m_j(Y_j)}$. (D.3)

D.4 Total PCR6

$m_{\text{PCR6}}(X) = m_\cap(X) + \sum_{i=1}^S \Delta_i(X)$. (D.4)

D.5 Verification of Mass Conservation

Summing (D.4) over $X$:

$\sum_X m_{\text{PCR6}}(X) = \sum_X m_\cap(X) + \sum_X \sum_i \Delta_i(X)$.

The first term equals $1 - K_{\text{tot}}$ by (D.1) and (D.2). The second term must equal $K_{\text{tot}}$. This holds because each conflicting configuration is counted in exactly one $\Delta_i$ term for each participating source, and the weights sum to the configuration's mass. The formula in (C.4) is mass-conserving.

D.6 Complexity

The outer sum over $X$ has $|G^\Theta|$ terms. For DST, $|G^\Theta| = 2^{|\Theta|}$. For DSmT, $|G^\Theta| = D_{|\Theta|}$.

The inner sum over $i$ has $S$ terms. For each, the inner sum over $(Y_j)_{j \neq i}$ has $|G^\Theta|^{S-1}$ terms in the worst case (with pruning by the disjointness condition).

Total worst-case operations:

$O\big(|G^\Theta| \cdot S \cdot |G^\Theta|^{S-1}\big) = O\big(S \cdot |G^\Theta|^S\big)$. (D.5)

For DST, $|\Theta| = 4$, $S = 6$:

$|G^\Theta| = 16$, $S \cdot 16^6 = 6 \cdot 1.68 \times 10^7 \approx 10^8$ operations.

For DSmT, $|G^\Theta| = 168$, the cost is prohibitive: $6 \cdot 168^6 \approx 10^{14}$. The architectural response is to restrict to DST for the fusion layer, or to use the DSmT free model only for mass assignment, not for fusion.

D.7 Numerical Example ($S = 3$)

Let $\Theta = \{a, b, c\}$, and let

$m_1(\{a\}) = 0.6, \; m_1(\{a,b\}) = 0.4$,
$m_2(\{b\}) = 0.5, \; m_2(\{b,c\}) = 0.5$,
$m_3(\{c\}) = 0.7, \; m_3(\{a,c\}) = 0.3$.

The conjunctive consensus collects all intersections:

$m_\cap(\{a\} \cap \{b\} \cap \{c\}) = 0.6 \cdot 0.5 \cdot 0.7 = 0.21 \to \varnothing$ (conflict),
$m_\cap(\{a\} \cap \{b\} \cap \{a,c\}) = 0.6 \cdot 0.5 \cdot 0.3 = 0.09 \to \{a\}$,
$m_\cap(\{a\} \cap \{b,c\} \cap \{c\}) = 0.6 \cdot 0.5 \cdot 0.7 = 0.21 \to \{c\}$,
$m_\cap(\{a\} \cap \{b,c\} \cap \{a,c\}) = 0.6 \cdot 0.5 \cdot 0.3 = 0.09 \to \{a,c\}$,
$m_\cap(\{a,b\} \cap \{b\} \cap \{c\}) = 0.4 \cdot 0.5 \cdot 0.7 = 0.14 \to \varnothing$ (conflict),
$m_\cap(\{a,b\} \cap \{b\} \cap \{a,c\}) = 0.4 \cdot 0.5 \cdot 0.3 = 0.06 \to \{a\}$,
$m_\cap(\{a,b\} \cap \{b,c\} \cap \{c\}) = 0.4 \cdot 0.5 \cdot 0.7 = 0.14 \to \{c\}$,
$m_\cap(\{a,b\} \cap \{b,c\} \cap \{a,c\}) = 0.4 \cdot 0.5 \cdot 0.3 = 0.06 \to \{c\}$.

Total conflict $K_{\text{tot}} = 0.21 + 0.14 = 0.35$.

PCR6 redistributes. For $X = \{a\}$, source $i=1$ contributes from configurations where $X_1 = \{a\}$ and $\{a\} \cap Y_2 \cap Y_3 = \varnothing$. This includes $(Y_2, Y_3) = (\{b\}, \{c\})$ with mass $0.5 \cdot 0.7 = 0.35$. Contribution:

$\frac{0.6^2 \cdot 0.35}{0.6 + 0.5 + 0.7} = \frac{0.126}{1.8} = 0.07$.

Similar contributions accumulate from other sources. The exact computation is performed in the reference implementation.

