Appendix F — Credal Sets and Imprecise Probability

F.1 Definition

A credal set $\mathcal{K}$ is a closed convex set of probability measures on a measurable space $(\Omega, \mathcal{F})$.

F.2 From Belief Function to Compatible Probability Set

Given a belief function $\text{Bel}$ on $\Theta$, the compatible probability set is

$\mathcal{P}(\text{Bel}) = \{p : p(A) \geq \text{Bel}(A) \; \forall A \subseteq \Theta\}$. (F.1)

This is a polytope with vertices at the extreme points of the belief-function core. Equivalently,

$\mathcal{P}(\text{Bel}) = \{p : \text{Bel}(A) \leq p(A) \leq \text{Pl}(A) \; \forall A \subseteq \Theta\}$. (F.2)

F.3 Credal Set from Copula Family

$\mathcal{K}_{ij} = \operatorname{cl\,conv}\!\left(\bigcup_{\theta \in \mathcal{C}_{\text{adm}}^{ij}} \mathcal{P}(\text{Bel}_{m_\theta})\right)$. (F.3)

The closure and convex hull ensure $\mathcal{K}_{ij}$ is a genuine credal set.

F.4 Lower and Upper Expectations

For a bounded function $f: \Theta \to \mathbb{R}$:

$\underline{E}(f) = \inf_{p \in \mathcal{K}} \mathbb{E}_p[f]$, $\overline{E}(f) = \sup_{p \in \mathcal{K}} \mathbb{E}_p[f]$. (F.4)

The indicator $f = 1_H$ gives $\overline{E}(1_H) = \sup_{p \in \mathcal{K}} p(H)$.

F.5 Robust Safety Condition

The central safety condition is

$\sup_{P \in \mathcal{K}_k} P(H_i \mid O_{1:k}) \leq \epsilon_i$. (F.5)

F.6 Finite-Extremal-Copula Approximation

Restrict $\Theta_{\text{copula}}$ to a finite set $\{C_1, \ldots, C_m\}$ containing the bounds $C^-, C^+, \Pi$ and a finite $\varepsilon$-net in the sup norm. Define

$\mathcal{K}_C^{\text{fin}} = \operatorname{conv}\!\left(\bigcup_{\ell=1}^m \mathcal{P}(\text{Bel}_{C_\ell})\right)$. (F.6)

This is a polytope. Worst-case optimization over a polytope is an LP.

F.7 Approximation Error

If the finite net satisfies $\sup_{u,v} |C_\theta(u,v) - C_{\ell}(u,v)| \leq \varepsilon$ for every $\theta$, then

$|Q(\mathcal{K}_C^{\text{fin}}) - Q(\mathcal{K}_C)| \leq \varepsilon \cdot 2^{|\Theta|}$. (F.7)

For $|\Theta| = 4$, the factor is 16. Acceptable error bounds then require $\varepsilon \leq 10^{-3}$ for $10^{-2}$-level error.

