Appendix H — Invariant Proof Sketches

H.1 Inv_Auth: $\square(D = \text{DEPLOY} \Rightarrow A = \text{AUTHORIZED})$

Proof sketch. The only action that sets $D' = \text{DEPLOY}$ is Deploy, which requires A = "AUTHORIZED" in its guard. No other action modifies D to DEPLOY. A is unchanged by Deploy. Therefore any state with $D = \text{DEPLOY}$ has $A = \text{AUTHORIZED}$.

H.2 Inv_Uncertainty: $\square(P = \text{UNCERTAIN} \Rightarrow D = \text{POSTCHECK})$

Proof sketch. $P' = \text{UNCERTAIN}$ is set only by Timeout and by the Environment mechanical-fault disjunct, both of which set $D' = \text{POSTCHECK}$. A' in those actions is unchanged from the previous state. The invariant holds by inspection.

H.3 Inv_HoldBound: $\square(A = \text{HOLD} \Rightarrow t_{\text{hold}}[i] < t_{\text{hold}}^{\text{max}})$

Proof sketch. EnterHold requires t_hold[i] < t_hold_max in its guard before setting A' = "HOLD". Hold increments t_hold[i] and requires t_hold[i] < t_hold_max before incrementing, so the incremented value is at most t_hold_max. But A is unchanged by Hold. If t_hold[i] reaches t_hold_max, Abort becomes enabled and sets A' = "INHIBITED". Therefore whenever A = "HOLD", t_hold[i] < t_hold_max.

H.4 Inv_Evidence: $\square(D = \text{DEPLOY} \Rightarrow \text{EvidenceOK})$

Proof sketch. Deploy requires EvidenceOK in its guard and preserves it. The Environment disjunct for force-exit fires when ~EvidenceOK and sets D' = "POSTCHECK". Therefore any state reached with $D = \text{DEPLOY}$ was reached via Deploy or preserved from a prior state, and in both cases $\text{EvidenceOK}$ holds.

H.5 Inv_NoCaptive: $\square\neg(P = \text{CAPTIVE} \land D = \text{DEPLOY})$

Proof sketch. Deploy requires P = "CAPTIVE" in its guard but sets P' = "SEPARATING" simultaneously. So the post-state has $P = \text{SEPARATING}$, $D = \text{DEPLOY}$, and the invariant is not violated. No action sets P' = "CAPTIVE" while D = "DEPLOY".

H.6 Inv_TerminalShape: $\square(D = \text{DONE} \Rightarrow i = N + 1)$

Proof sketch. D = \text{DONE} is set only by ConfirmSeparation when i = N, at which point i' = i + 1 = N + 1. i is unchanged thereafter. Therefore any state with $D = \text{DONE}$ has $i = N + 1$.

H.7 Inv_NoDeployHold: $\square\neg(D = \text{DEPLOY} \land A = \text{HOLD})$

Proof sketch. Deploy requires A = "AUTHORIZED" in its guard. EnterHold requires D \in \{"PRECHECK", "ARMED"\}. Therefore A = "HOLD" and D = "DEPLOY" cannot be simultaneously established by any action.

H.8 Candidate Liveness Under Environment Assumption

Under the assumption that Environment eventually stops injecting faults and eventually supplies Verdict = "AUTHORIZE":

$\Diamond\square(\text{env\_fault} = \text{"NONE"} \land \text{EvidenceOK} \land \text{Verdict} = \text{"AUTHORIZE"})$.

Then Arm, Deploy, ConfirmSeparation fire under their fairness assumptions, and the mission reaches $D = \text{DONE}$. Without this assumption, no liveness property of termination is provable.

