Appendix J — Authorization Epoch Semantics

J.1 Epoch Structure

An authorization epoch is a tuple

$e_i = (i, \nu_i, t_i, \mathcal{E}_i, \text{model}_i)$ (J.1)

where

· $i$ is the payload identifier,
· $\nu_i \in \mathbb{N}$ is the epoch counter,
· $t_i$ is the authorization timestamp,
· $\mathcal{E}_i$ is the evidence snapshot identifier,
· $\text{model}_i$ is the decision-kernel version identifier.

J.2 Epoch Freshness

$\text{fresh}(e_i)$ iff $t_i > t_{i-1}$ and $\mathcal{E}_i \neq \mathcal{E}_{i-1}$ and $\nu_i > \nu_{i-1}$.

J.3 Deployment Implication

$Deploy_i \Rightarrow \text{epoch}(A_i) = e_i \land \text{payload}(A_i) = i \land \text{fresh}(e_i)$. (J.2)

J.4 Non-Inheritance Invariant

$Deploy_i \Rightarrow \text{epoch}(A_i) = \text{epoch}_i \land \text{epoch}_i \neq \text{epoch}_{i-1} \quad (i > 1)$. (J.3)

J.5 Refinement in TLA⁺

In the TLA⁺ module, the epoch is implicit in the action structure: Arm sets A = "AUTHORIZED", ResetAuth returns A to UNAUTHORIZED, and the sequence of actions ensures a new authorization is issued for each payload. To make the epoch explicit, add a variable epoch with type Nat and require:

Arm increments epoch,
ResetAuth preserves epoch,
Deploy requires epoch > 0.

Then Inv_NonInherit becomes:

Inv_NonInherit == [](D = "DEPLOY" => epoch > 0 /\ epoch > epoch_of(i-1)).

For the current module, the implicit structure is sufficient because the sequence of actions forces a fresh authorization per payload.

J.6 Evidence Snapshot Semantics

The evidence snapshot $\mathcal{E}_i$ is a versioned hash of the sensor data used in Decision. It is not a TLA⁺ variable in the current module; it is an assumption of the Layer C interface. A future extension may model it explicitly.

