Appendix K — Inertia Uncertainty Propagation: Detailed Derivation

K.1 Setup

Let $\theta = (m_s, r_s, \text{vec}\, I_s^{\text{cm}}) \in \mathbb{R}^{10}$ be the parameter vector for the separated payload: mass $m_s$, center-of-mass position $r_s$, and 9 components of the inertia tensor $I_s^{\text{cm}}$.

Let $F(\theta) = \text{vec}\, I'_{\text{CG}}$ be the mutated inertia tensor of the remaining vehicle, expressed as a 9-vector.

K.2 Three-Step Decomposition

$F = T \circ S$, where

$S(\theta)$: subtracts the payload contribution from the current inertia and mass,

$T$: applies the parallel-axis correction to re-express the inertia about the new CG.

K.3 Step 1: Subtraction

$m' = m - m_s$, (K.1)

$I_{\text{remaining}} = I_{\text{old}} - I_s^{\text{cm}} - m_s [(r_s - r_{CG})^\top (r_s - r_{CG}) I_3 - (r_s - r_{CG})(r_s - r_{CG})^\top]$. (K.2)

K.4 Step 2: New CG

$r_{CG}' = \frac{m \cdot r_{CG} - m_s \cdot r_s}{m'}$. (K.3)

K.5 Step 3: Parallel-Axis Shift

$I'_{\text{CG}} = I_{\text{remaining}} + m' [(r_{CG}' - r_{CG})^\top (r_{CG}' - r_{CG}) I_3 - (r_{CG}' - r_{CG})(r_{CG}' - r_{CG})^\top]$. (K.4)

K.6 Jacobian

$J_F = \frac{\partial \text{vec}\, T}{\partial \text{vec}\, I} \cdot \frac{\partial \text{vec}\, S}{\partial \theta} + \frac{\partial \text{vec}\, T}{\partial d} \cdot \frac{\partial d}{\partial \theta} + \frac{\partial \text{vec}\, T}{\partial m_s} \cdot e_{m_s}^\top$, (K.5)

where $d = r_{CG}' - r_{CG}$ is the shift vector.

K.7 First-Order Propagation

$\Sigma_{I'} \approx J_F \Sigma_\theta J_F^\top$. (K.6)

K.8 Second-Order Remainder

$R_2(\theta) = \frac{1}{2} (\theta - \theta_0)^\top \nabla^2 F(\xi) (\theta - \theta_0)$ for some $\xi$ on the segment from $\theta_0$ to $\theta$. (K.7)

Bound:

$\mathbb{E}[\|R_2(\theta)\|] \leq \frac{1}{2} \sup_\xi \|\nabla^2 F(\xi)\| \cdot \text{tr}(\Sigma_\theta)$. (K.8)

K.9 Assumptions

1. $F$ twice continuously differentiable on a convex neighborhood of $\theta_0$.
2. $\Sigma_\theta$ exists and is finite.
3. $\|\nabla^2 F\|$ bounded on the support.
4. Matrix and vector norms explicitly specified.

K.10 Correlations to Include

The covariance matrix $\Sigma_\theta$ must include:

· Correlations among $m_s, r_s, I_s^{\text{cm}}$ (same-payload correlations).
· Uncertainty in $I_{\text{old}}$ and $r_{CG}$ (pre-mutation states).
· Dispenser translation state (if the dispenser indexes between payloads).

The current formulation covers only the first; the remaining two are registered as OP10.8 and OP10.13.

K.11 Status

Conditional local propagation bound. Not a general uncertainty-propagation theorem.

