Appendix L — Collision Risk: Union Bound and Assumptions

L.1 Pairwise Collision Probability

For payload $i$ and constellation member $j$, the two-dimensional collision probability at closest approach is

$P_c(i, j) = \frac{1}{2\pi \sigma_x \sigma_y} \exp\!\left(-\frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{x^2}{\sigma_x^2} + \frac{y^2}{\sigma_y^2}\right)\right) \cdot A_{\text{combined}}$, (L.1)

where $A_{\text{combined}}$ is the combined hard-body cross-section, $(x, y)$ is the projected miss vector at closest approach, and $\sigma_x, \sigma_y$ are the projected covariances.

L.2 Union Bound

For a set of collision events $\{H_j\}_{j \in \mathcal{C}_i}$, the probability of at least one collision is

$P\!\left(\bigcup_j H_j\right) \leq \sum_j P(H_j)$. (L.2)

Equality holds if the events are mutually exclusive, which is not generally the case for collisions with different constellation members (they can overlap in time).

L.3 Union-Bound Surrogate

Define

$U_{\text{coll}}(i) = \sum_{j \in \mathcal{C}_i} P_c(i, j)$. (L.3)

This is the union-bound surrogate, a conservative upper bound on the aggregate collision probability.

L.4 Threshold Semantics

$U_{\text{coll}}(i) \leq P_{c,\text{aggregate}} = 10^{-3}$ is a budget constraint on the union-bound surrogate. It is not a physical probability constraint. The corresponding physical probability is at most $10^{-3}$ under the union bound.

L.5 NASA CARA Thresholds

· $P_c > 10^{-4}$: mitigation action required.
· $P_c > 10^{-7}$: operational attention.
· Post-mitigation target: $P_c < 3 \times 10^{-6}$.

These are screening thresholds for individual conjunctions, not for aggregate constellation risk. The aggregate budget $P_{c,\text{aggregate}} = 10^{-3}$ is a separate architectural choice (OP4).

L.6 Covariance Realism

The collision probability depends critically on the covariance estimates $\sigma_x, \sigma_y$. NASA CARA emphasizes covariance realism: the covariance used in the calculation must reflect the actual uncertainty, not a nominal value. Correlated errors between the payload and constellation members further complicate the calculation.

L.7 Limitations

The current formulation assumes:

· Pairwise two-dimensional conjunction geometry.
· Independent covariance for each pair.
· No temporal correlation between conjunctions.
· No joint collision dynamics.

These are standard assumptions in operational collision screening but are not verified in this architecture.

