Appendix M — State-Space Analysis

M.1 Decomposition

$|\mathcal{Q}| = |\mathcal{P}| \cdot |\mathcal{D}| \cdot |\mathcal{F}| \cdot |\mathcal{A}| \cdot |\mathcal{E}| \cdot |\mathcal{I}| \cdot |\mathcal{T}|$, (M.1)

where $\mathcal{T}$ is the hold-array space.

M.2 Factor Cardinalities

$|\mathcal{P}| = 4$, $|\mathcal{D}| = 5$, $|\mathcal{F}| = 3$, $|\mathcal{A}| = 4$, $|\mathcal{I}| = N + 1$.

$|\mathcal{T}| = (t_{\text{hold}}^{\text{max}} + 1)^{N+1}$.

$|\mathcal{E}|$ is continuous; in the abstract model, it is not counted.

M.3 Discrete-State Count

$|\mathcal{Q}_{\text{disc}}| = 4 \cdot 5 \cdot 3 \cdot 4 \cdot (N+1) \cdot (t_{\text{hold}}^{\text{max}} + 1)^{N+1} = 240 (N+1) (t_{\text{hold}}^{\text{max}} + 1)^{N+1}$. (M.2)

M.4 $N = 26$, $t_{\text{hold}}^{\text{max}} = 10$

$|\mathcal{Q}_{\text{disc}}| = 240 \cdot 27 \cdot 11^{27} \approx 240 \cdot 27 \cdot 5.05 \times 10^{28} \approx 3.27 \times 10^{32}$. (M.3)

M.5 Reachability Reduction

Most of this space is unreachable. The set $C$ is redundant with $i$ on every reachable state, reducing the effective space. The hold array is monotone within a payload's authorization: $t_{\text{hold}}[i]$ is incremented only while $A = \text{HOLD}$ and reset to zero on Arm and ResetAuth. This reduces the effective hold-array space.

M.6 Assume-Guarantee Decomposition

Per-payload contracts are verified in isolation:

· Phase $i$: precondition is the state after payload $i-1$'s ConfirmSeparation.
· Phase $i$: postcondition is the state at payload $i$'s ConfirmSeparation.
· Composition: the postcondition of phase $i$ must imply the precondition of phase $i+1$ (which is exactly the identity by construction).

Under this decomposition, the effective verification state space is $\sim 240 \cdot 11$ per payload, and the composition is by induction over $i$.

