Appendix O — Open Problems: Detailed Statements

OP1. Scalable verification for $N > 100$

Statement. Exhaustive TLC verification of the discrete kernel is intractable for $N > 100$. Assume-guarantee decomposition reduces the per-phase state space, but the composition proof and its inductive argument remain to be formalized.

OP2. Calibration of $\theta_N, \theta_H, \theta_U, \Gamma_{\text{max}}, w_K, w_\rho$

Statement. The thresholds are architectural parameters. Their values must be derived from mission-specific safety requirements, statistical calibration, and possibly regulatory constraints. No derivation is provided.

OP3. Instantiation of TLA⁺ variables

Statement. Verdict, ProjectedPc_x1e6, and related abstract variables must be instantiated against the physical and evidential layers. The refinement relation $R$ specifies the required conditions but does not give an explicit instantiation.

OP4. Aggregate collision budget

Statement. $P_{c,\text{aggregate}} = 10^{-3}$ is a union-bound budget. Its derivation from first principles (constellation size, mission profile, regulatory constraint) is not provided.

OP5. Which uncertainty representation preserves safety properties

Statement. DST, DSmT, and copula-restricted credal sets preserve different safety properties. Which representation is appropriate for which safety claim is an open question.

OP6. Human-in-the-loop

Statement. The role of human operators in the authorization decision is not modeled. A human-in-the-loop variant would require additional TLA⁺ structure.

OP7. Quantitative reliability model for the Pez mechanism

Statement. No quantitative reliability model exists for the Pez dispenser. Such a model is required for a compliant FMECA.

OP8. Probabilistic model of flatellite parameters

Statement. No public probabilistic model exists for $(m_s, r_s, I_s^{\text{cm}})$ for a flatellite. The inertia uncertainty propagation is conditional on the existence of such a model.

OP9. Copula parameter estimation

Statement. Estimating copula parameters from residual data is a statistical problem with its own uncertainty. The tolerance $\delta$ in the admissibility condition absorbs this uncertainty but does not eliminate it.

OP10. Per-payload DSK instantiation vs shared

Statement. Whether the DSK should be instantiated per payload or shared across payloads is an architectural choice with implications for state-space size and evidence reuse.

OP11. (Resolved) $S = 6$ always

Statement. Resolved in v5.0. The Layer C source count is $S = 6$, independent of payload count.

OP12. Adversarial environment coverage

Statement. The adversarial environment in the TLA⁺ module covers fault injection, evidence loss, and phase exit. Whether the coverage is sufficient for safety verification is not established.

OP13. Body-frame origin and dispenser translation

Statement. The body-frame origin convention and the dispenser translation between payloads must be specified. The current inertia model assumes a static origin.

OP14. Hybrid-automaton embedding of continuous evidence

Statement. The continuous evidence layer is not embedded in the discrete TLA⁺ kernel. A hybrid-automaton embedding would allow richer verification.

OP15. LP feasibility and conditioning

Statement. The finite-extremal-copula approximation yields a polytope. LP feasibility and conditioning depend on the structure of the polytope, which is not characterized.

OP16. Calibration of $\delta$, $\Theta_{\text{copula}}$, $\varepsilon$-net density

Statement. The tolerance $\delta$ and the copula family $\Theta_{\text{copula}}$ are architectural choices. Their calibration is not addressed.

OP17. Non-emptiness of the joint copula family

Statement. For $S = 6$ sources, the joint copula family $\mathcal{C}^{(6)} = \{C_{1:6} : \operatorname{marg}_{ij}(C_{1:6}) \in \mathcal{C}_{\text{adm}}^{ij} \; \forall i < j\}$ may be empty. The pairwise admissibility condition is necessary but not sufficient. This is blocking for any global fusion claim.

OP18. Error bound of the finite-extremal-copula approximation

Statement. The bound $|Q(\mathcal{K}_C^{\text{fin}}) - Q(\mathcal{K}_C)| \leq \varepsilon \cdot 2^{|\Theta|}$ requires the finite net to be an $\varepsilon$-net. The construction of such a net for the specific copula family is not given.

OP19. Proof of the refinement relation

Statement. The refinement relation $R(s_{\text{phys}}, s_{\text{abs}})$ is stated but not proved. The proof requires physical argument for each abstract state condition.

OP20. Authorization epoch semantics under partial evidence updates

Statement. When evidence updates occur without a full epoch change, the semantics of the authorization epoch are unclear. A partial-update policy is not defined.

