```
   Orbit plane; candidate payload i+1 against constellation C_i

     C_1  o
          \        projected relative motion of i+1
           \       ----------------------------->
            \    /
             \  /
              X   <-- closest approach; miss vector r = (x, y)
             / \
            /   \
     C_2  o       o  C_3

     Hard-body combined radius:    R_HB = R_{i+1} + R_j
     Projected covariance ellipse: sigma_x, sigma_y

     Pairwise probability:

        P_c(i+1, j) = (1/(2 pi sigma_x sigma_y)) * exp(-Q/2) * A_HB

     Obligations:

        O1:   max_j P_c(i+1, j) <= P_c_screen      = 1e-4
        O2:   U_coll(i+1) = sum_j P_c(i+1, j) <= P_c_aggregate = 1e-3

     U_coll is a UNION-BOUND SURROGATE, not a physical probability:

        P( union_j H_j )  <=  sum_j P(H_j)
```

Figure 9. Pairwise screening is exact; the aggregate obligation is a conservative budget on the union-bound surrogate U_coll.

