Figure 10 — TLA⁺ Action Structure (as a Dependency Graph)

```
   Actions (disjuncts of Next):

     Environment : drives env_fault', EvidenceOK', F', Verdict', Pc', P' (forced)
     Arm         : D : PRECHECK -> ARMED ;  A := AUTHORIZED ;  t_hold[i] := 0
     EnterHold   : A := HOLD                (D unchanged)
     Reevaluate  : A : HOLD -> AUTHORIZED or UNAUTHORIZED   (Verdict != HOLD)
     Deploy      : D : ARMED -> DEPLOY ;  P : CAPTIVE -> SEPARATING
     ConfirmSep  : P : SEPARATING -> SEPARATED ;  i := i+1 ;  C := C U {i} ;
                   D : DEPLOY -> POSTCHECK (i < N) or DONE (i = N)
     ResetAuth   : D : POSTCHECK -> PRECHECK ;  A := UNAUTHORIZED ;  P := CAPTIVE
     Timeout     : P : SEPARATING -> UNCERTAIN ;  D : DEPLOY -> POSTCHECK
     Hold        : t_hold[i] := t_hold[i] + 1
     Abort       : P := CAPTIVE ;  D := POSTCHECK ;  A := INHIBITED
     Disposal    : UNCHANGED vars  (stutter when D = DONE)

   Enabling graph:

        Environment -----------------------> all actions (guards read env vars)
        Arm -------------------------------> EnterHold, Deploy
        EnterHold ------------------------> Hold, Reevaluate
        Reevaluate -----------------------> Deploy
        Deploy ---------------------------> ConfirmSep, Timeout, Abort
        ConfirmSep -----------------------> ResetAuth, Disposal
        ResetAuth ------------------------> Arm   (next payload)
        Timeout --------------------------> ResetAuth, Abort
        Abort ----------------------------> ResetAuth
```

Figure 10. Every action reads at least one variable derived from the Environment disjunct. Liveness of the mission is therefore conditional on an environmental assumption of eventual fault-free operation.

